  "details": "I've been messing around with launching enemy actors with physics particles, but have run into a number of snags. For starters, unity won't launch an AI if they still have their navmesh agent component enabled, as I demonstrate in the gif below\nhttps://gyazo.com/6656ba7e015232e9a544ae2e4c1c78bd\n\nDespite disabling the navmesh on particle collision, vrchat still acts as though the navmesh is enabled when the enemy is shot.\nhttps://gyazo.com/11b2fe6ed535ec071490fae63a04dcd6\n\nTo further complicate things, I brought an AI into the scene with the navmesh disabled by default, the AI target far away and up in the air a little, and turned off the AI and controllers on particle collision. worked as expected in unity, but in vrchat it somehow did this\nhttps://gyazo.com/0ce427b78b777a777d4c3cee95adc9f6\n\nI have no idea how this is happening. Nothing special is happening when I shoot the enemy according to the log. (ignore the exceptions, they'd take too long to explain)",
